    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0821" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/3–2847: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-28T10:00:00+01:00">March 28, 1947—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:24 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>491. Source in Fabrique Nationale states company is still awaiting opening of
                    letter of credit by Chinese Government for shipment munitions (Deptel 223,
                    February 24). Source states does not know reasons for withholding letter of
                    credit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
